From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Quarrier <squarrier@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 20:02:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] glm5_next/cuda: the --parallel pool compacts before it
 evicts, TF_GLM_COMPACT_BEFORE_EVICT (MiaAI-Lab recipe patch 0074)

A request, or a decoding stream's extent, that needed rows the pool had free but not in one range evicted kept
prompts, least recently used first, until a free range opened, and compacted only after evicting every one, so two
long conversations taking turns at a nearly full pool evicted each other's kept prompt (the recipe's issue #61).
MiaAI-Lab's recipe v1.6 compacts as soon as the free rows cover the request, with patch 0074-glm-compact-before-evict:
for a growing extent, the extents up to it slide down and the ones after it up, so the free rows follow it (each
moves once at most), and it evicts only while the free rows fall short. Placement only: the same replies. This ports
it behind a switch of this tree's own, off by default:

- multi.py: MultiDecoder.compact_first (TF_GLM_COMPACT_BEFORE_EVICT); _compact(grow=None), verbatim (without grow,
  the same moves as before); _room's and _grow's loops of the patch, run when the switch is on. TF_GLM_CACHE_ROOM=1,
  this tree's own room rule (cache_room), still makes the room when it is set, with or without this switch.
- engine.py: a startup line when the switch is on.
- tests/glm_pool_room_check.py: the recipe's tools/pool_room_check.py (0074's checks, by ezoushen), verbatim.
- THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md: "GLM compact before evict".

Unset, _room and _grow take the same paths as before.

Tests: tests/test_glm_compact_first.py (12, CPU): the switch; the recipe's checks on this tree's MultiDecoder: all pass
with the switch on, and off the same five fail as on the recipe's tree just before 0074 (its tree at 68ebd67 passes
all); two ranks over the fake model, off and on: a new prompt with the free rows in pieces (off: the two oldest kept
prompts go; on: the extents move and all stay and resume), a kept prompt taken over in place that must grow into its
neighbour's block (off: the neighbour's prompt goes; on: the extents after it move up, nothing is evicted, and the
neighbour's next turn resumes), growing streams over a fragmented pool (every row survives the moves; on evicts no
more than off), llama-benchy's runs in a scaled pool (on misses no more than off), and TF_GLM_CACHE_ROOM=1 with it
(cache_room makes the room). Every reply equals the request served alone; both ranks hold the same pools.

Credit: patch 0074 was written by ezoushen (https://github.com/ezoushen) in
MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold pull request #62 (issue #61), and MiaAI-Lab applied it as
contributed in recipe commit 5859365 (v1.6), Apache License 2.0, with tools/pool_room_check.py.

Changed from the picked commit: tests/test_glm_cache_room.py's off cases run with TF_GLM_COMPACT_BEFORE_EVICT unset
(they check the recipe's room rule as of patch 0030), and tests/test_glm_compact_first.py's tests run with
TF_GLM_CACHE_ROOM unset unless a test sets it: each test checks one room rule with the other rule's switch unset.

